==Swedish==

===Etymology 1===
From ''o-'' ([[un-]], [[miss-]]; prefix used for negation) + ''[[van]]'' ([[accustomed]] to)

====Pronunciation====
* {{audio|Sv-ovan.ogg|audio}}

====Adjective====
{{sv-adj-reg}}
'''ovan'''

# not [[used]] to, inexperienced, lacking practice

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|gmq-osw|sv}} ''ovan'' ({{etyl|non|sv}} {{term|ofan|lang=non}}).
Cognate with Danish {{term|oven|lang=da}} and German {{term|oben|lang=de}}, as well as with the compound forms Dutch {{term|boven|lang=nl}} and English {{term|above|lang=en}}.

====Preposition====
'''ovan'''

# [[above]], at some unspecified point of higher altitude
#: ''Högt '''ovan''' molnen'' = ''High above the clouds''

